// error
// #3444, epic #2185: an unknown field or method on a LITERAL receiver passes
// `bit check` silently and only fails later, at lowering, with a spanless
// "cannot lower" refusal. #2106/#2641 already reject this for a VARIABLE
// receiver (`f.zzz` where `f: f64`) with a real E0057 — the split was
// specifically literal vs. variable, because a literal types as one of the
// UntypedInt/UntypedFloat/... constant kinds (checkExprType), never the
// concrete Prim kind the pre-#3444 validator required.
//
// Reachable without anyone writing a deliberate literal member access: `0..len(s)`
// lexes as `0.` `.len(s)` — a float-literal receiver — so the range-loop
// spelling a Go/Rust/Python user writes first hit exactly this hole.
fn main() {
  let y = 1.5.zzz
  let z = "a".zzz
  let w = (5).zzz
  println("${y}${z}${w}")
}
